 "description": "On October 20, 2026, Elon Musk said on SpaceX's earnings call that SpaceX and Tesla have each formed special committees of independent directors to discuss a possible merger. Together they are worth roughly $3.5 trillion at current market values. No terms have been agreed. We go through what was said, SpaceX's Q3 numbers (AI is now its biggest business), Tesla's Q3 results, why supporters like the idea, why pension funds and critics worry about control, how a Tesla shareholder vote would work, and what happens next. Stick figures, facts only.\n\nDave and Linda are made-up characters. Real people are shown as generic labelled stick figures; quotes are attributed as reported. Not financial advice.\n\nSources:\nTechCrunch, SpaceX and Tesla boards form special committees to review merger (Oct 20, 2026): https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/20/spacex-and-tesla-boards-form-special-committees-to-review-merger/\nAxios, SpaceX, Tesla explore merger, Elon Musk confirms (Oct 20, 2026): https://www.axios.com/2026/10/20/spacex-tesla-merger-talks\nFortune, SpaceX posts first operating profit as public company as AI revenue nearly triples (Oct 20, 2026): https://fortune.com/2026/10/20/spacex-q3-profit-ai-si-elon-musk/\nFortune, Musk's $3.5 trillion Tesla-SpaceX merger talks put his accountability to the test (Oct 21, 2026): https://fortune.com/2026/10/21/elon-musk-trillionaire-spacex-tesla-merger-corporate-accountability/\nYahoo Finance, Musk backs SpaceX-Tesla merger idea as both boards form special committees: https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/article/musk-backs-spacex-tesla-merger-idea-as-both-boards-form-special-committees-113219080.html\nElectrek, Tesla Q3 2026 financial results (Oct 21, 2026): https://electrek.co/2026/10/21/tesla-tsla-q3-2026-financial-results/\nInvesting.com, Tesla Q3 2026 earnings call transcript: https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-tesla-beats-q3-2026-estimates-as-stock-slips-after-hours-93CH-4964365\n\n#t